# Structured inspection

`--json` should describe live tmux sessions and discovered repository checkout
candidates with identities suitable for strict lifecycle commands.

    :bins jj cat sh sed

> [!NOTE]
> 'jj', 'cat', 'sh', and 'sed' are available.

    :copy tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)

    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :$ jj git init alpha (exit: 0)
    :$ jj workspace add -R alpha --name feature alpha.feature (exit: 0)

Create a live session attached to the default checkout, flag it, and publish an
agent state that requires attention. The runner session remains a plain live
session, while the named workspace is a non-live candidate discovered by the
glob.

    :t new-session -d -s alpha-live -c alpha "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -F -t '=alpha-live:' @smth.repo '#{pane_current_path}' (success)
    :t set-option -t '=alpha-live:' @smth.flag 1 (success)
    :t set-option -p -t alpha-live:0.0 @smth.agent.state waiting (success)

    :$ sh -c 'smth --no-base --repo "alpha*" --json | sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
[
  {
    "name": "runner",
    "tmux": "runner",
    "live": true,
    "deletable": false,
    "flagged": false
  },
  {
    "base": "<ROOT>/alpha",
    "path": "<ROOT>/alpha",
    "tmux": "alpha-live",
    "live": true,
    "deletable": false,
    "flagged": true,
    "attention": [
      "0"
    ],
    "agents": {
      "waiting": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "base": "<ROOT>/alpha",
    "name": "feature",
    "path": "<ROOT>/alpha.feature",
    "tmux": "alpha/feature",
    "live": false,
    "deletable": true
  }
]
```

The same fuzzy matcher used by the picker should narrow structured output, and
an unmatched query should emit an empty JSON array even with `--exit-0`.

    :$ sh -c 'smth --no-base --repo "alpha*" --query feature --json | sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
[
  {
    "base": "<ROOT>/alpha",
    "name": "feature",
    "path": "<ROOT>/alpha.feature",
    "tmux": "alpha/feature",
    "live": false,
    "deletable": true
  }
]
```

    :$ smth --no-base --repo "alpha*" --query zzz --json --exit-0 (exit: 0)

```stdout
[]
```

JSON inspection must not combine with line-oriented filtering or automatic
session selection.

    :$ smth --json --filter (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--json' cannot be used with '--filter'

Usage: smth --json

For more information, try 'help'.
```

    :$ smth --json --select-1 (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--json' cannot be used with '--select-1'

Usage: smth --json

For more information, try 'help'.
```

